          "question_type": "APPSC 2024 PYQ Pattern (How Many Correct)",
          "question": "With reference to Governor's Legislative Powers (Articles 200 & 213), consider the following three statements:\n1. Under Article 200, when a State Bill is presented to the Governor, the Governor may give assent, withhold assent, return the Bill (if it is not a Money Bill) for reconsideration, or reserve the Bill for the consideration of the President.\n2. Under Article 213, the Governor can promulgate Ordinances only when the State Legislature (or either House in a bicameral legislature) is not in session; such ordinances must be approved by the State Legislature within six weeks of its reassembly.\n3. A Governor can return a State Money Bill for reconsideration under Article 200 and promulgate ordinances even when both Houses of the State Legislature are in session.\n\nHow many of the statements given above are correct?",
