          "explanation": "Only Statement 1 is correct.\n• Statement 1 is correct: The Godavari River (Dakshin Ganga, total length ~1,465 km) enters Andhra Pradesh and forms a vast lobate delta below Rajamahendravaram (Dowleswaram Barrage built by Sir Arthur Cotton in 1852); its major left-bank tributaries include Purna, Pranhita, Indravati, and Sabari, while Manjira is a major right-bank tributary.\n• Statement 2 is incorrect because: The Polavaram Project (Indira Sagar) is a multi-purpose National Irrigation Project on the Godavari River near Ramayyapeta village, designed to transfer 80 TMC of surplus Godavari water to the Krishna river basin via the Right Main Canal (Pattiseema/Prakasam Barrage link). (The claim that 'The Godavari River originates in the Aravalli Range and flows westward into the Arabian Sea without forming any delta.' is factually false).",
