            "In the Balance of Payments (BoP), software service exports and private remittances from the Indian diaspora are recorded under the 'Invisibles' (Services and Transfers) sub-account of the Current Account, whereas FDI and FPI inflows are recorded under the Capital/Financial Account.",
            "Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) inflows and external commercial borrowings are part of the Merchandise Trade balance in the Current Account.",
            "Official records under RBI Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy document key provisions on Balance of Payments & Foreign Exchange Reserves."
