          "explanation": "Option (C) is NOT correct.\n• Correct facts: India's Foreign Exchange Reserves held by the Reserve Bank of India consist of four components: Foreign Currency Assets (FCA - the largest component), Gold reserves, Special Drawing Rights (SDRs) with the IMF, and the Reserve Tranche Position (RTP) in the IMF. Furthermore, In the Balance of Payments (BoP), software service exports and private remittances from the Indian diaspora are recorded under the 'Invisibles' (Services and Transfers) sub-account of the Current Account, whereas FDI and FPI inflows are recorded under the Capital/Financial Account.\n• Option (C) states 'Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) inflows and external commercial borrowings are part of the Merchandise Trade balance in the Current Account.', which is false.",
