          "question_type": "Analytical & Quantitative",
          "question": "Under a Self-Help Group (SHG) linkage programme, Rs. 1,44,000 is distributed among three groups P, Q, and R in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. How much more amount does Group R receive than Group P?",
          "options": [
            "Rs. 18,000",
            "Rs. 24,000",
            "Rs. 36,000",
            "Rs. 48,000"
          ],
          "correct_index": 1,
          "explanation": "Step-by-step calculation:\n• Total ratio parts = 3 + 4 + 5 = 12 parts.\n• Value of 1 part = Rs. 1,44,000 / 12 = Rs. 12,000.\n• Difference between Group R (5 parts) and Group P (3 parts) = 5 - 3 = 2 parts.\n• Required difference = 2 × Rs. 12,000 = Rs. 24,000.",
