          "question_type": "Statement Elimination",
          "question": "With reference to Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) & RBI, consider the following statements:\n1. Under Section 45ZB of the amended RBI Act, 1934, the Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) is a six-member statutory body (3 from RBI including the Governor as ex-officio Chairperson, and 3 external members appointed by the Central Government) tasked with maintaining price stability while keeping in mind the objective of growth.\n2. The Monetary Policy Committee consists of 10 members chaired by the Union Finance Secretary and targets Wholesale Price Index (WPI) inflation at 2%.\n\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?",
          "options": [
            "1 only",
            "2 only",
            "Both 1 and 2",
            "Neither 1 nor 2"
          ],
          "correct_index": 0,
          "explanation": "Only Statement 1 is correct.\n• Statement 1 is correct: Under Section 45ZB of the amended RBI Act, 1934, the Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) is a six-member statutory body (3 from RBI including the Governor as ex-officio Chairperson, and 3 external members appointed by the Central Government) tasked with maintaining price stability while keeping in mind the objective of growth.\n• Statement 2 is incorrect because: The flexible inflation targeting framework mandates maintaining Consumer Price Index (CPI-Combined) inflation at 4% with a tolerance band of +/- 2% (i.e., 2% to 6%). The RBI Governor holds a casting vote in case of a tie. (The claim that 'The Monetary Policy Committee consists of 10 members chaired by the Union Finance Secretary and targets Wholesale Price Index (WPI) inflation at 2%.' is factually false).",
